// endpoint_report_view_dwell.proto — ReportViewDwell: the editor has started,
// or stopped, counting how long the user has viewed this workspace. HOST
// section.
//
// Emacs is the only sender, because dwell is an editor fact: it is the only
// process that knows the workspace's panels are on screen and how long the
// user has stood in front of them, and it alone chooses the dwell's length.
// MarkWorkspaceViewed is the dwell's VERDICT, sent once the count completes;
// this verb is the count's PROGRESS, so the webapp sidebar can carry the row's
// name continuously from its unviewed colour to the viewed grey over exactly
// the dwell (frontend.v1.RosterRowViewDwell) instead of flipping when the
// verdict lands.
//
// ONE REPORT IN FLIGHT PER WORKSPACE. Two reports for one workspace sent
// concurrently could be served out of order, and a stop served after the
// count that followed it would end a dwell that is still running. So the
// editor sends a workspace's next report only once the previous one is
// answered, and sends its latest state then: the daemon serves a
// workspace's reports in the order the editor decided them.
//
// IDEMPOTENT: a counting report replaces the workspace's standing dwell, and a
// stopped report for a workspace with no dwell is a success that changes
// nothing.

